1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:09,000
Maya CRM: a CRM that lets businesses answer
their Facebook Page messages from one inbox.

2
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:18,000
Settings > Messenger. No Facebook Page is connected yet.

3
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Clicking 'Connect with Facebook' opens Facebook Login.
The user reviews and grants: pages_show_list,
pages_messaging and pages_manage_metadata.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:36,000
pages_show_list: the user picks the Page
they want to manage in Maya.

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Maya lists the Pages the user manages.
The selected Page is now connected (name and ID shown).

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:54,000
pages_manage_metadata: 'Subscribe webhook' subscribes
this Page to the 'messages' webhook field.

7
00:00:55,000 --> 00:01:03,000
A customer sends a message to the Page
from Messenger (right side).

8
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:12,000
The webhook event arrives: the new conversation
from the same Page appears in Maya's inbox.

9
00:01:13,000 --> 00:01:21,000
pages_messaging: the business agent replies
from Maya and clicks Send.

10
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
The reply sent from Maya is delivered
in the customer's Messenger (native client).

11
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Both messages are stored in Maya's conversation.
End of demo.
